# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file
version: v1.25.1

# Paths excluded from `snyk code test`.
#
# .claude/ holds Claude Code's own skill scripts (design/brand/token
# tooling). They are developer utilities run locally with arguments the
# developer supplies, and they are never bundled into the deployed site.
# Snyk Code reported 20 "Path Traversal" notes there - a CLI argument
# choosing which file the developer's own script reads is not an attack
# path. Scanning them buries real application findings in noise.
#
# Excluding them from analysis is not the same as approving them. If any of
# these scripts is ever imported by app/, components/ or lib/, remove this
# exclusion and scan them properly.
exclude:
  code:
    - .claude/**

# Accepted risks.
#
# Accepted by Khaleed on 2026-10-21 so production can get Sentry while the
# Next 16 upgrade is done separately. Each entry expires on 2026-11-20. When
# it does, `snyk test` fails again and the deploy gate in CLAUDE.md is closed
# until the finding is fixed or explicitly re-accepted. Never extend these
# just to make a scan pass.
#
# The same next@15.5.28 is already live in production, so accepting these
# does not add exposure; it stops the gate from also holding back Sentry.
ignore:
  SNYK-JS-NEXT-15105315:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2025-59472. Requires PPR or cacheComponents together with
          NEXT_PRIVATE_MINIMAL_MODE; this app uses neither. Fix is the Next 16
          upgrade, tracked separately.
        expires: 2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-21T04:30:00.000Z
  SNYK-JS-NEXT-15674556:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-27980. Image optimizer disk cache; the app has zero
          next/image imports and Vercel runs its own managed image
          optimization. Fix is the Next 16 upgrade, tracked separately.
        expires: 2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-21T04:30:00.000Z
  SNYK-JS-NEXT-20569640:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-94544. Requires the 'use cache' directive together with
          draft mode; the app uses neither. Fix is the Next 16 upgrade,
          tracked separately.
        expires: 2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-21T04:30:00.000Z
  SNYK-JS-NEXT-20569641:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-94543. The upstream advisory lists 15.5.27 as fixed, so
          this looks like an overlapping version range; accepted rather than
          relied on. Fix is the Next 16 upgrade, tracked separately.
        expires: 2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-21T04:30:00.000Z
  SNYK-JS-PICOMATCH-21248802:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-112366, ReDoS. picomatch 4.0.7 is the latest release and
          has no fix. Reached only via @sentry/nextjs > @rollup/plugin-commonjs,
          a build-time bundler plugin matching globs from our own config; no
          user input reaches it at runtime. Re-check when a fixed picomatch or
          @sentry/nextjs ships.
        expires: 2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-21T04:30:00.000Z
